<title>AUSTRALIA: Coal and Allied half yr loss jumps.</title>
<headline>Coal and Allied half yr loss jumps.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit	  loss    7.29  vs  8.14 loss</p>
<p>    Net			   loss    8.76  vs  4.58 loss</p>
<p>    Interim dividend (cents)	   nil  vs   nil</p>
<p>NOTE: Coal and Allied Industries Ltd is a coal mining group and is about 70 percent owned by Rio Tinto Plc/Ltd.  </p>
<p>    Sales				 258.71  vs 275.79</p>
<p>    Other income			 11.13  vs  11.76</p>
<p>    Abnormal			loss 10.00  vs   nil</p>
<p>    Tax			    credit 8.53  vs credit 3.57</p>
<p>    Interest				1.18  vs   3.12</p>
<p>    Depreciation			 30.33  vs  24.57</p>
<p>    Minorities			    0.03  vs   0.01</p>
<p>    Shrs (cents)		  loss  13.8  vs loss 7.2</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
